<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Codex Argenteus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Silver Bible</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Codex Argenteus, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">Silver</a> Bible, is a 6th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gospels">Gospels</a> in the Gothic translation made by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulfilas">Wulfila</a>, written in silver and gold ink on purple parchment, probably in Ravenna under the Ostrogothic king Theodoric. It is the main surviving source for the Gothic language. Kept for centuries at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/werden">Werden</a> Abbey, it later passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> and was taken by Swedish troops in 1648; it is now at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppsala-university">Uppsala University</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/codex-argenteus.jpg" alt="Codex Argenteus" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Magnus Hjalmarsson · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Codex_argenteus_-_Cover.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Bible was translated among the Visigothic Christians of Moesia, while the <b>Codex Argenteus</b> was preserved and passed on by northern Ostrogoths in present-day Italy.</blockquote><a href="/language/gothic">Gothic · Speakers &amp; Spread</a></li><li><blockquote>Its library held the <b>Codex Argenteus</b>, the silver Bible of the Gothic language, before it passed to Prague and later Uppsala.</blockquote><a href="/state/imperial-abbey-of-werden">Imperial Abbey of Werden</a></li></ul></section>
